# Domain `__NAME__`

Generated by `python -m maaos create-domain __NAME__`. Guide: `docs/domains/ADDING_A_DOMAIN.md`.

| File | Role | You edit |
|---|---|---|
| `types.py` | value types: `State`, `Call`, `Task` (+ `identities()`) | the objects, actions and goal of your domain |
| `model.py` | the optimistic symbolic model: `project`, `apply`, `applicable`, `plan`, `apply_world` | the intended effects and preconditions |
| `environment.py` | the backend boundary: `_reset`, `_attempt`, `_is_terminal` | how actions really execute (the only module that may import a backend) |
| `__init__.py` | the declaration `DOMAIN` (tasks, examples, recovery advice) | tasks, examples, recovery |

Check it: `python -m maaos validate-domain __NAME__` (after adding the registry lines it prints).
Run the generated test: `python -B -m unittest __TEST_MODULE__`.
